kadran: unknown command "bilinmeyen"

kadran dev — Kadran workstation tool

Usage:
  kadran <command> [options] [target]

Commands:
  status [target]                              shows server and daemon status
  app <create|update|list|show|delete> …       manages app definitions
  deploy <app> [target]                        builds a commit and switches traffic to it
  rollback <app> [target]                      switches traffic back to the previous release
  logs [-f] <app> [target]                     streams the live release's output
  prune [-dry-run] <app>|-all [target]         removes old releases' containers
  alarms [target]                              lists active fault conditions
  backup <create|list> [target]                takes and lists database backups
  domain check <domain> [target]               checks a domain's DNS, ports and certificate
  audit <list|verify> [target]                 reads and verifies the audit chain
  server <add|list|rm|rename> …                manages the saved server list
  sidecar                                      stdio JSON-RPC server for the desktop app
  bootstrap root@server | -sudo user@server    installs or upgrades the server
  github <connect|status|disconnect> [target]  connects private GitHub repositories
  key <list|add|remove> … root@server          manages deploy-only keys
  login [-recovery] [target]                   signs in with a TOTP code (when TOTP is on)
  logout [target]                              deletes the saved sign-in for a server
  totp <status|enable|disable|reset> [target]  manages two-step sign-in
  version                                      prints version information

Target forms:
  (empty)                   local socket — /run/kadran/api.sock
  /path/api.sock            local socket, explicit path
  user@server               SSH (default user: kadran-client)
  user@server:2222          SSH, custom port
  server                    SSH, default user
  -s name                   a server saved with kadran server add

Exit codes:
  0  success
  1  error (could not connect, chain could not be verified)
  2  usage error
  3  audit chain BROKEN — possible tampering

Options go after the command and before the target:
  kadran audit list --limit 20 user@server
